course: dictionary
lesson: 9864
title: Syrian: a place, a person, or a hamster
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Syrian can work as a describing word, like Syrian food, or as a naming word, like a Syrian. Look at the words around it to see which job it is doing. Syrian tells you where someone or something comes from.
explain: A Syrian is a person from Syria. «Many Syrian families found new homes in Canada.» Here Syrian describes the families, and they came from Syria.
explain: Context can also show you a different meaning. «Syrian hamsters live alone in the wild and attack other hamsters.» Syrian is not a person here. It names a kind of hamster, because the word hamsters comes right after it.
fact: Syria is a country in the Middle East, on the east coast of the Mediterranean Sea.
fact: Syria borders Turkey, Iraq, Jordan, Lebanon and Israel.
fact: The capital of Syria is Damascus, one of the oldest cities in the world.
fact: «Syrian» can be an adjective, as in «Syrian food», or a noun, as in «a Syrian», which means a person from Syria. The plural is «Syrians».
fact: «Adult Syrian hamsters fight, sometimes badly, so each one lives alone.» That is why each hamster must have its own cage.
exercise: «Adult Syrian hamsters fight, sometimes badly, so each one lives alone.» In this sentence, what is Syrian? | A country on the Mediterranean | *A kind of hamster | A person from Syria | A type of food
exercise: What is a Syrian? | A city with the capital Damascus | *A person from Syria | A country in the Middle East | A sea on the map
exercise: Syria is on the east coast of which sea? | North Sea | Red Sea | *Mediterranean Sea | Caspian Sea
test: Which word names a country? | Damascus | hamster | Syrian | *Syria
test: Which country borders Syria? | Spain | Canada | Egypt | *Turkey
exam: What is the capital of Syria? | *Damascus | Aleppo | Beirut | Amman
